  {
   "approach": "From the Whitney Portal trailhead, follow the Whitney Trail a short way to the North Fork of Lone Pine Creek, where a climbers' trail leaves it and climbs a wooded slope into a willow-choked valley. Where the valley tightens, a third-class chute in the canyon wall leads onto the Ebersbacher Ledges, which skirt the worst of the brush and end at Lower Boy Scout Lake. Continue past Upper Boy Scout Lake over slabs, talus and moraine, then up a gully through the last band of cliffs to Iceberg Lake, the usual camp for the east side. From the lake, go on up the bowl to the foot of the big east face. The climb begins between the bushy cracks and If At First, left of the latter. A Whitney Zone permit from Inyo National Forest is required: a day-use permit for a car-to-car push, or an overnight North Fork permit if you camp.",
